# Claude Code project guide — ADDF Light Games (optional)

> **Only install as a new CLAUDE.md or carefully merge into an existing file.** Do not blindly overwrite human-owned project instructions.

This game project follows **ADDF Light Games**.

1. Before inspecting arbitrary files, read `SECURITY.md`.
2. Read `AGENTS.md` as the durable operating contract, then `STATE.md` to find the current stage/status. Read `GAME.md`, `DECISIONS.md`, `planning/BACKLOG.md`, and active sprint files only when needed.
3. Human design decisions (Gate D), exact implementation authorization (Gate I), and human acceptance (Gate A) are separate and cannot be supplied by AI.
4. Source edits, commands, packages, public deployment and asset changes require the exact scoped authorization in the active `PLAN.md`; new scope requires re-approval. Separate special permission is needed for destructive, public, paid and sensitive operations.
5. Never self-accept tests or infer consent from a prior chat. Report one next safe step and stop at each human checkpoint.
6. For detailed workflow assistance, use the installed `/addf-light-games` project skill when available.

These instructions are *additive*; they do not weaken local security policy, repository restrictions or human commands.
